## Reference only
- astryx (`meta/astryx`, MIT): React and StyleX design system; the site is plain HTML with Tailwind.
- Mika (`wangzan101/mika`, Apache-2.0): Android agent over ADB or wireless debugging. Not on Carlos's phone; Maestro flows cover the test phone.
- unslop (`heydamir/unslop`, CC-BY-4.0): overlaps Hallmark. Pick one: Hallmark.
- Zero-Breach-Toolkit (`interplains/Zero-Breach-Toolkit`, Apache-2.0, #4016): offline triage of a personal Mac or phone for spyware, stalkerware and open doors. It does not scan app code, APKs or QR-pairing APIs, so it does not harden CursorQuota. Anonymous publisher; embedded datasets carry mixed licenses (CC BY, CC BY-SA, DRL-1.1) and `--make-iphone-backup` pulls GPL-3.0 `pymobiledevice3`. Never run it on Carlos's devices without his consent (Full Disk Access, USB debugging). Patterns worth reading only: `scan/zbtriage/netguard.py` (socket guard) and `CONTRACT.md`.

